{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pose suggest review --path pose-mcp; rg -n 'read.view|audit|deadline' .pose/knowledge --glob '*.md' | head -60; rg -n '\"'^(artifact'\"\\\\.|surface\\\\.|\\\\[.\\\\].*(error|pass)|.*(error|exit|verdict|strict).*)' /var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"# POSE trail — review\n\nAvaliação técnica de PR/diff: escopo, contratos, segurança, validação.\n- Path:      pose-mcp → domain: backend-go (repo-map)\n- Workflow:  .pose/workflows/review.md\n- Skill:     pose-review\n- Rules:     .pose/rules/security.md, .pose/rules/documentation-style.md, .pose/rules/backend-go.md\n- Spec:      false\n- ADR:       false\n- Knowledge: consume=true, produce=handoff (quando aceitar risco residual ou condicionar merge)\n- Validation: exigir evidência de pose validate do implementador\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:72:locale (templates default en `knowledge.md`/`doc-audit-report.md` estavam\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:214:  auditoria trimestral agendada (`governance-audit.yml`), evidência real em\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:271:- Primeira auditoria trimestral (2026-10-01) precisa de revisão humana e\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:26:Review within 90 days, or before introducing transactional storage or persisted refusal auditing. The 90-day TTL covers the consolidation rollout rather than changing durable rules.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:34:@pose-maintainers reviews changes to persistence or audit contracts.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:10:  spec: \"spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:14:    - \"pose lint-spec pose-governance-read-view-generation --strict\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:32:em cascata. D7 e a emenda aceita no ADR definem coordenador auditado e views\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:41:`work/governance-read-view-recovery`, base publicada `7079eb86`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:105:- Writers externos e uma edição A→B→A que desaparece antes da auditoria não\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:118:- [Spec B34](../specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:120:- [Start atual](../starts/pose-governance-read-view-generation.json)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:43:B13 e read views B34 permanecem nos respectivos escopos.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:10:  spec: \"pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:31:across the audit's trial runs, depending on which other specs had most\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:36:Fixed the trigger only (spec `pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes`, R7):\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:76:follow-up (spec `pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes`, Follow-ups) is picked up.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:80:- spec:pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes (Decision 2, R7, Non-goals)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:28:The Unix backend propagates flock errors unchanged. A synthetic overlay returning syscall.EOPNOTSUPP, with only the wait bound reduced from two minutes to 200 ms, reached the deadline in 201 ms and reported another conclusion holding the lock. It published zero proofs and attestations. This is injected error-path evidence, not a claim that the local filesystem lacks flock. Evidence: .review-work/round4/permanent.log, permanent-overlay.json, permanent_lock.go and permanent_wait.go (local, untracked).\n/var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out:1:surface.spec=pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\n/var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out:2:surface.targets=1\n/var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out:3:surface.results=233\n/var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out:4:surface.findings=0\n/var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out:5:surface.provenance_digest=sha256:459eb8d73ca6b3f976ac726b4dcc9c51d431c58b0df853a04f0715e8d093ee96\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:1:artifact.spec=pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:2:artifact.change_set=cs-4bd6fb70856f\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:3:artifact.change_set.base=d49d3aeb4ed8daa2b44b2c46d8ce5536d39dc199\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:4:artifact.change_set.head=f72cf7e3adb4652acb432d1fa64192421db8a8e0\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:5:artifact.change_set.commits=15\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:6:artifact.diff_digest=sha256:a5dc7ce6e9342054576cd8494dd980b4c42e1519c1e141634b53867ead4422f7\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:7:artifact.claims=4\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:8:artifact.observed=21\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:9:artifact.findings=976\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:58:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/check_verdict_mode_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:517:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:835:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/usage/verdict.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:943:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:1411:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:2383:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_verdicts_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:2548:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/usage/verdict_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:2608:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/change_set_single_pass_test.go\n/var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out:2677:[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json.go\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files .pose/specs | rg 'read-view-audit'; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; cat .pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md | tail -55\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files .pose/specs | rg 'read-view-audit'; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; cat .pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md | tail -55\"","aggregated_output":".pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time.md\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\nseeding/indexação, identidade explícita das fontes federadas e diagnóstico Git.\nNada disso torna prova histórica em autorização atual.\n\nNotas locais de recuperação e logs estão em `recovery-notes/`, excluídos do Git.\nUse os resultados nativos atuais e os commits com trailer da spec como evidência\npublicável; não promova os relatos históricos deste handoff a testes atuais.\n\n## Next checks\n\n1. Registrar D6 e compilar seu CLI exato; repetir o índice real antes da matriz.\n2. Executar a matriz nativa completa, incluindo Go, integração com `-race`,\n   build, vet e checks de segurança aplicáveis.\n3. Reconciliar artifacts e trace, commitar a implementação com o trailer\n   `POSE-Spec`, compilar o CLI atual e gerar a evidência nativa da matriz.\n4. Passar artifact-check, surface-check e check estrito. Só então selar o bundle\n   e obter revisão de uma execução separada que não implementou o código final.\n5. Aplicar o closeout nativo, repetir os gates pós-fechamento e publicar sem\n   forçar o histórico. O CI remoto está dispensado nesta tarefa.\n\nPara Go nesta máquina, usar o cache padrão e `GOTMPDIR`/`TMPDIR` em\n`/var/tmp/pose-work-go` com a autorização de filesystem aplicável. O cache\ndescartável `/tmp/pose-b34-go-cache` esgotou a quota e foi limpo; não recriá-lo.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Não converter controles positivos de `current` em `unknown` para esconder\n  falhas; tampouco promover índice legado ou prova histórica a autorização atual.\n- Preservar o contrato de verificação histórica: metadado atual desconhecido\n  não equivale automaticamente à invalidação de uma aprovação histórica;\n  autoridade, trust e fontes necessárias ilegíveis ou revogadas continuam\n  bloqueando o que seu contrato exigir.\n- Um diretório comprovadamente sem Git pode sustentar um build de índices\n  exclusivamente de filesystem; inputs materiais de refs/histórico continuam\n  exigindo a prova Git correspondente.\n- Limites recalibrados em D6: 25.000 registros agregados, 512 MiB de inputs,\n  8 MiB de metadados, 16 roots, profundidade federada oito e uma repetição.\n  D5 conserva 64 arestas de dependência e 256 identidades/entradas por grafo/lista.\n  A calibração reteve 18.905 registros e cerca de 353,5 MiB em memória; não publicou\n  índices e não equivale aos gates normais. Nenhum truncamento certifica completude.\n- Writers externos e uma edição A→B→A que desaparece antes da auditoria não\n  recebem garantia transacional. O fencing só cobre participantes do protocolo.\n- O assessment de dívida lido nesta tarefa foi incompleto: duas specs históricas\n  inválidas não puderam ser lidas. Não reportar esse scan como completo.\n\n## Next owner\n\n@pose-maintainers. A coordenação mantém integração e gates. Use `pose delegate`\npara trabalho secundário e somente `gpt-6.1-sol` com reasoning médio, conforme\na orientação do usuário. Sucesso de task não é revisão governada ou atestação.\n\n## References\n\n- [Spec B34](../specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md)\n- [ADR aceito](../adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md)\n- [Start atual](../starts/pose-governance-read-view-generation.json)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
