{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/2026-11-17-pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time.md; cat .pose/starts/pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time.json'","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-17\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer a auditoria final da read view repetir cada leitura de Git capturada sob um prazo com o mesmo tempo que a leitura teve, contado a partir da auditoria, em vez do instante absoluto em que o prazo da leitura venceu.\n\n### Business value\nO `pose index` do pose-dist passou a reprovar sempre com \"index inputs changed during generation\". Instrumentado, mostrou que cada `git show --binary` da integridade de entrega (`changeSetGitStream`, prazo de 2 minutos por leitura) era repetido na auditoria com o instante absoluto do prazo; a geração do índice já leva cerca de 135 s, então os primeiros streams chegavam à auditoria vencidos, falhavam com \"context deadline exceeded\" e eram contados como entradas mudadas. Toda operação mais longa que o prazo de uma das suas leituras reprova assim, e o índice do pose-dist cresce a cada spec. Isso parou o pipeline de fechamento de `pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph` duas vezes.\n\n### Constraints\n- A repetição da auditoria continua limitada no tempo.\n- Uma leitura que de fato mudou continua sendo reportada.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Mudar o prazo das leituras.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: The final audit shall repeat every captured Git command and every streamed Git read that was captured under a deadline with a timeout equal to the time the read had (its deadline less its start), counted from the audit.\n- R2: An unchanged read audited after its own deadline shall not be reported as changed or unknown.\n- R3: A read captured with a deadline already past shall be audited with a minimal positive timeout.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhum custo novo: a auditoria só troca o contexto da repetição.\n\n### Security\n- A repetição continua limitada; nenhuma leitura passa a rodar sem prazo.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Leituras sem prazo continuam sem prazo na auditoria.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/governance_read_view_git.go`: comandos capturados guardam o tempo que tiveram; a auditoria repete sob esse tempo.\n- `pose/governance_read_view_stream.go`: o mesmo para leituras em stream.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_audit_timeout_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por toda operação de read view que audita leituras de Git com prazo: `pose index`, fechamentos e revisões. Check permanente `read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestReadViewAudit|TestAuditTimeoutIsTheTimeTheReadHad' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Uma auditoria com muitas leituras lentas pode levar até a soma dos prazos delas; isso já valia dentro do prazo de cada uma.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Tempo da leitura guardado na captura e usado na repetição (R1, R3).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste com leitura e stream capturados sob prazo curto e auditados depois dele, com prova de reprovação; `pose index` no clone do pose-dist.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-17\n- Context: o `pose index` do pose-dist reprovava sempre depois que a geração passou de 2 minutos.\n- Options considered: (a) repetir com o tempo que a leitura teve, a partir da auditoria; (b) repetir sem prazo; (c) aumentar o prazo das leituras.\n- Decision: (a).\n- Basis: R1, R2, R3\n- Rationale: (b) tira o limite da repetição; (c) só adia o problema para um índice maior; (a) mantém a repetição limitada como a leitura foi.\n- Consequences: a auditoria de uma operação longa não depende mais da duração da operação.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTeste com uma read view real: um comando e um stream capturados sob prazo de 2 s, auditados 2,5 s depois; medição do `pose index` no clone do pose-dist.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-17\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, Git 2.56; clone do pose-dist em d49d3aeb.\n- Notes: o `pose index` do clone reprovou três vezes seguidas; a auditoria instrumentada mostrou `git show --binary` repetidos com \"context deadline exceeded\" depois do prazo absoluto de 2 minutos. Com a correção o índice foi escrito em 135 s. Os testes do comando (`ls-tree -r -z HEAD`, que não é leitura pura e a auditoria repete) e do stream reprovam cada um quando só a sua correção é revertida, e um terceiro mostra que um HEAD movido depois do prazo continua reportado como mudança.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: o `pose index` do pose-dist volta a escrever; leituras inalteradas não viram mudança depois do prazo.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadViewAuditRepeatsACommandUnderItsOwnTime test:TestReadViewAuditRepeatsAStreamUnderItsOwnTime test:TestReadViewAuditStillSeesAChangeAfterTheDeadline check:read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestReadViewAuditRepeatsACommandUnderItsOwnTime test:TestReadViewAuditRepeatsAStreamUnderItsOwnTime\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestAuditTimeoutIsTheTimeTheReadHad\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-8ff5d2cdc744047e, changes-requested): F1 o teste capturava `ls-tree -r -z <id completo>`, que o motor classifica como leitura pura e a auditoria não repete; ele passava mesmo com a correção dos comandos revertida. Agora há um teste por tipo de leitura, com `ls-tree -r -z HEAD` (repetido pela auditoria) e um stream, cada um reprovando quando só a sua correção é revertida, e um teste que move o HEAD depois do prazo para provar que a repetição acontece.\n\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"spec\": \"pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n  \"plan_digest\": \"ca80c0709b105f9d0caa61f88b61fe42f4ff207b95289f345e4b9fba1be40060\",\n  \"revision\": \"06a41c7e5cfb45ea275e2f9b9ca80810a5f03a62\",\n  \"spec_digest_before\": \"21ad788d266ce983553fc82c86a527948c8e75d384d7c7085ba2fe787f879485\",\n  \"spec_digest_after\": \"14a53a7ab953e7b47c9babbd2fb8d6f98affb7af31ee52aaa49b9a4e4fa2c3b3\",\n  \"baseline\": {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n    \"nodes\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"R1\",\n        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n        \"hash\": \"7f73f3b5e62f\",\n        \"state\": \"active\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"R2\",\n        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n        \"hash\": \"5908555026fd\",\n        \"state\": \"active\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"R3\",\n        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n        \"hash\": \"c20ce5e28171\",\n        \"state\": \"active\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D1\",\n        \"kind\": \"decision\",\n        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time\",\n        \"hash\": \"3676acec0dac\",\n        \"state\": \"active\",\n        \"relations\": [\n          \"R1\",\n          \"R2\",\n          \"R3\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"digest\": \"sha256:31c9bc791046f4671bb9cc0a19296bc9342b3d6c643aee1dc597e91a8c2c225a\"\n  },\n  \"phase\": \"started\",\n  \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-17T01:35:17Z\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'func governancePureGitRead|func governanceHeadAt|func changeSetGitStream' pose-mcp/internal/pose; sed -n '350,430p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1215,1255p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1,150p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture.go; rg -n 'WithDeadline|\\\\.deadline' pose-mcp/internal/pose --glob '*.go' | head -70\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'func governancePureGitRead|func governanceHeadAt|func changeSetGitStream' pose-mcp/internal/pose; sed -n '350,430p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1215,1255p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1,150p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture.go; rg -n 'WithDeadline|\\\\.deadline' pose-mcp/internal/pose --glob '*.go' | head -70\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_pure.go:22:func governancePureGitRead(args []string) (byObject, byHead bool) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_pure.go:72:func governanceHeadAt(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string) string {\n\tfor ancestor := path; ; ancestor = filepath.Dir(ancestor) {\n\t\tif project, ok := op.rootProjectByPath[ancestor]; ok {\n\t\t\treturn project, ancestor\n\t\t}\n\t\tparent := filepath.Dir(ancestor)\n\t\tif parent == ancestor {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", \"\"\n}\n\nfunc (v *governanceReadView) markUnknownIf(condition bool, producer, reason string) {\n\tif condition {\n\t\tv.markUnknown(producer, reason)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) audit() governanceReadViewAudit {\n\tresult := governanceReadViewAudit{ChangedProducers: map[string]bool{}, UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn result\n\t}\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\troots := append([]*governanceReadViewRoot(nil), op.roots...)\n\tinitialRoots := op.initialRoots // Immutable after beginGovernanceReadView returns.\n\tinitialConflicts := op.initialConflicts\n\tcurrentRoots := op.currentRoots\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\tperRoot := map[*governanceReadView]governanceReadViewAudit{}\n\tauditBudget := &governanceReadViewAuditBudget{}\n\tfor _, root := range roots {\n\t\tif _, done := perRoot[root.view]; done {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tperRoot[root.view] = root.view.auditSingleWithBudget(auditBudget)\n\t}\n\tchanged := []string{}\n\tfor _, audit := range perRoot {\n\t\tchanged = append(changed, audit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\tfor producer, value := range audit.ChangedProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = value\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor producer, reasons := range audit.UnknownProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = append(result.UnknownProducers[producer], reasons...)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif op.git != nil {\n\t\tgitAudit := op.git.audit()\n\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, gitAudit)\n\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n\t\tchanged = append(changed, gitAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\tfor producer, value := range gitAudit.ChangedProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = value\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor producer, reasons := range gitAudit.UnknownProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = append(result.UnknownProducers[producer], reasons...)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif currentRoots != nil {\n\t\tcurrent, conflicts, overBudget := currentRoots()\n\t\tif overBudget || !sameStringMap(initialRoots, current) || !sameBoolMap(initialConflicts, conflicts) {\n\t\t\tregistryAudit := governanceReadViewAudit{UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n\t\t\treason := \"authorized root registry changed during the operation\"\n\t\t\tif overBudget {\n\t\t\t\treason = \"authorized root registry exceeded its bounded final-audit budget\"\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedPaths = []string{\"authorized-roots\"}\n\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedProducers = map[string]bool{\"projection\": true}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tregistryAudit.UnknownProducers[\"projection\"] = []string{reason}\n\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&result, registryAudit)\n\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, registryAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\t\t// Metadata and the captured proof are assembled from these root\n\t\t\t// audits. Keep the operation-wide registry observation on the\n\t\t\t// primary root too, so it cannot disappear after the bounded retry.\n\t\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, registryAudit)\n\t\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n\t\t}\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\treturn filepath.Clean(path)\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.Clean(name)\n}\n\nfunc (v *governanceReadView) begin() error {\n\tv.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer v.mu.Unlock()\n\tif v.closed {\n\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewFinalized\n\t}\n\tv.active++\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (v *governanceReadView) end() {\n\tv.mu.Lock()\n\tv.active--\n\tif v.active == 0 && v.cond != nil {\n\t\tv.cond.Broadcast()\n\t}\n\tv.mu.Unlock()\n}\n\nfunc (v *governanceReadView) displayPath(path string) string {\n\trel, err := filepath.Rel(v.root, path)\n\tif err == nil && rel != \"..\" && !strings.HasPrefix(rel, \"..\"+string(filepath.Separator)) {\n\t\treturn filepath.ToSlash(rel)\n\t}\n\treturn \"external:\" + digestBytes([]byte(filepath.Clean(path)))\n}\n\nfunc (v *governanceReadView) markUnknownLocked(producer, reason string) {\n\tif producer == \"\" {\n\t\tproducer = \"projection\"\n\t}\n\tif v.unknown[producer] == nil {\n\t\tv.unknown[producer] = map[string]bool{}\n\t}\n\tv.unknown[producer][reason] = true\npackage pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\nvar (\n\t// ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged means the captured input closure changed\n\t// and could not be certified after a failed callback or the permitted retry.\n\tErrGovernanceReadViewChanged = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view changed during capture\")\n\t// ErrGovernanceReadViewUnknown means the operation could not prove the\n\t// completeness of its captured input closure.\n\tErrGovernanceReadViewUnknown = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view input closure is unknown\")\n)\n\n// WithGovernanceReadView runs a read-only callback against one immutable view\n// and audits that view before returning. A changed view is retried once; if\n// the retry changes or any required observation is unknown, the callback must\n// not be used to publish a derived result. The callback must keep its outputs\n// in memory; publishers write through the caller's original guarded Store only\n// after this method succeeds.\nfunc (s Store) WithGovernanceReadView(producer string, run func(Store) error) error {\n\tif run == nil {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"pose: governance read view callback is required\")\n\t}\n\tif producer == \"\" {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"pose: governance read view producer is required\")\n\t}\n\treturn withGovernanceReadViewCaptureAttempt(s.withoutGovernanceReadView(), producer, 0, false, func(store Store) (bool, error) {\n\t\treturn true, run(store)\n\t})\n}\n\n// WithGovernanceReadViewForIndexBuild allows the callback to discover whether\n// the index inputs depend on a Git source revision. A missing primary HEAD is\n// captured and audited as data; the callback returns true when that revision\n// is semantically required by the generation it produced.\nfunc (s Store) WithGovernanceReadViewForIndexBuild(producer string, run func(Store) (requiresPrimaryRevision bool, err error)) error {\n\tif run == nil {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"pose: governance read view callback is required\")\n\t}\n\tif producer == \"\" {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"pose: governance read view producer is required\")\n\t}\n\treturn withGovernanceReadViewCaptureAttempt(s.withoutGovernanceReadView(), producer, 0, true, run)\n}\n\nfunc withGovernanceReadViewCaptureAttempt(s Store, producer string, attempt int, allowMissingPrimaryRevision bool, run func(Store) (bool, error)) error {\n\tbase, view := s.beginGovernanceReadView(allowMissingPrimaryRevision)\n\tstore := base.withGovernanceReadView(view, producer).PinIndexes()\n\tif !allowMissingPrimaryRevision {\n\t\t_, _ = captureGovernanceSourceRevision(store.fsys(), store.Root, producer)\n\t}\n\trequiresPrimaryRevision, err := run(store)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// A callback can translate a failed read into a domain error. Preserve\n\t\t// that error and the independently audited closure failure, without\n\t\t// retrying a callback that has already failed.\n\t\taudit := view.audit()\n\t\tauditErr := governanceReadViewUnknownError(audit)\n\t\tif governanceReviewAuditChanged(audit) {\n\t\t\tauditErr = errors.Join(auditErr, ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif auditErr == nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn errors.Join(err, auditErr)\n\t}\n\tif requiresPrimaryRevision {\n\t\tview.operation.requirePrimaryRevision(producer)\n\t}\n\taudit := view.audit()\n\tchanged := governanceReviewAuditChanged(audit)\n\tif changed && attempt == 0 {\n\t\treturn withGovernanceReadViewCaptureAttempt(base.withoutGovernanceReadView(), producer, 1, allowMissingPrimaryRevision, run)\n\t}\n\tif changed {\n\t\treturn ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged\n\t}\n\treturn governanceReadViewUnknownError(audit)\n}\n\n// Summaries contain producer labels and audit reasons, excluding observed paths\n// and the underlying path-bearing details of root/index resolution failures.\nfunc governanceReadViewUnknownError(audit governanceReadViewAudit) error {\n\tif len(audit.UnknownProducers) > 0 {\n\t\tproducers := make([]string, 0, len(audit.UnknownProducers))\n\t\tfor producer := range audit.UnknownProducers {\n\t\t\tproducers = append(producers, producer)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsort.Strings(producers)\n\t\tclip := func(value string, limit int) string {\n\t\t\tif len(value) <= limit {\n\t\t\t\treturn value\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn value[:limit-3] + \"...\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tvar summary strings.Builder\n\t\tfor i, producer := range producers {\n\t\t\tif i >= 8 {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&summary, \"; ... %d more producer(s)\", len(producers)-i)\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\t\tsummary.WriteString(\"; \")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsummary.WriteString(clip(producer, 128))\n\t\t\tsummary.WriteString(\": \")\n\t\t\treasons := append([]string(nil), audit.UnknownProducers[producer]...)\n\t\t\tsort.Strings(reasons)\n\t\t\tfor j, reason := range reasons {\n\t\t\t\tif j >= 4 {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&summary, \"; ... %d more reason(s)\", len(reasons)-j)\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif j > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\tsummary.WriteString(\" | \")\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfor _, prefix := range []string{\"index generation could not be pinned:\", \"authorized roots could not be resolved:\"} {\n\t\t\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(reason, prefix) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treason = strings.TrimSuffix(prefix, \":\")\n\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tsummary.WriteString(clip(reason, 256))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tdetail := summary.String()\n\t\tif len(detail) > 2048 {\n\t\t\tdetail = detail[:2045] + \"...\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %d producer(s) lack a complete observation: %s\", ErrGovernanceReadViewUnknown, len(audit.UnknownProducers), detail)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
